'' AN INTEGER CONSTANT ZERO OF ANY WIDTH -- '0l', 'cbyte( 0 )' -- reaches a pointer parameter, and an exact integer overload still wins (fbc's overload/pointers.bas const0). tiko took only pointer-width zeros (TKO0632). Expected output is fbc-modern's.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 tests/codegen/src/nullconst-to-ptr.bas -o tests/codegen/nullconsttoptr.exe
'' ENV: TKO_LIBPATH=toolchains/tiko-windows/lib/windows-x86_64
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' RUN: tests/codegen/nullconsttoptr.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: ptr-1
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: ptr-1
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: ptr-1
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: ptr-1
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: ptr-1
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: byte          any ptr       byte
